{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1446556-odd-lunar-animal-spirit-shapes","id":1446556,"title":"Odd lunar animal spirit shapes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-29T21:49:07-07:00","id":1446556,"title":"Odd lunar animal spirit shapes?","content":"Hello all, I was wondering if any of you have a selection of mutations that would make sense for a few lunar totems not mentioned in the book?<br /> <br /> -I have a Full Moon, and a No Moon, and both chose a Tanuki as their Spirit Shape. I was thinking something simple like, &quot;Silent Movement&quot;, &quot;Night Vision&quot;, &quot;Lure&quot; fluffy tail, &quot;Imposing Features&quot; the fluffy mane and their utter adorableness.<br /> <br /> -The other lunar is a monstrous horror, Bear + Crab monster, so I was thinking &quot;Carapace&quot;, &quot;Deadly Weaponry&quot; Chopping for pincers?, &quot;Natural Shield&quot;, &quot;Burrower&quot;. I suggest looking for the following pic. I am also unsure how you can get the special ability attacks of the monster beast in DBT? I assume you don't get to use Grasping Claws unless your in the crab shape itself?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.ca/pin/416160821794643374/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.ca/pin/416160821794643374/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.ca/pin/416160821794643374/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pinterest.ca/pin/416160821794643374/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","user":"Citadel97501","date":". 04-30-2021, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T02:55:06-07:00","id":1446576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1446556-odd-lunar-animal-spirit-shapes#post1446556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also unsure how you can get the special ability attacks of the monster beast in DBT?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't. Hybrid Body Transformation provides only Supernatural Merits, and Deadly Beastman Transformation provides some benefits atop that. Animal special abilities and Merits are accessible only be fully assuming their forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T05:48:07-07:00","id":1446588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1446556-odd-lunar-animal-spirit-shapes?p=1446576#post1446576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't. Hybrid Body Transformation provides only Supernatural Merits,</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear it provides <b>mutations</b> (which are defined as being <i>mundane or supernatural, innate or purchased</i> merits that modify the character's physical body) which reflect the spirit shape. These merits are found among those listed in the character traits sections.<br /> <br /> But, yes, an animal's Special Abilities and Merits can only be gained in the animal form - although mundane latent abilities need to be unlocked with experience or bonus points, and magical abilities cannot be accessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-30-2021, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T08:04:34-07:00","id":1446604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__